md='''# Optional body-proxy addendum: independent review\n\n**Pass as an optional, unadopted body-collision selection.** The completed Batch16 final receipt, report, proposed index and every existing asset remain unchanged. No art, export, mechanism or render revision was made.\n\n| Component | Detailed shapes | Optional body shapes | Omitted fine shapes | Greatest finite observed undercoverage | Separate conservative bound |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Audience seat | 43 | 13 | 30 | 56.520 mm | 72.002 mm |\n| Backstage stand | 56 | 30 | 26 | 35.000 mm | 48.002 mm |\n\nEvery retained shape dictionary is exactly equal to its frozen detailed counterpart, including source/native points and original moving ownership. All 16 primary floor, rest, work, grip, notes, emitter and control surfaces remain represented. Seven declared voids and full motion records are unchanged. Since identical transforms preserve subset inclusion at every pose, the selection cannot introduce an intrusion into the previously verified complete voids or movement paths. It does not retain the omitted fine mechanism contacts.\n\nOmissions are explicit: the seat excludes its bearing sectors, stubs, pins and retainers; the stand excludes corresponding aiming details plus its internal cable and three clips. Every retained/omitted material role and omitted extent was checked against the frozen semantic source. The omitted pieces remain visible, including exposed wiring in the service pose.\n\nThe independent finite measurements inspect every actual source-triangle vertex, edge midpoint and centroid at six seat poses and 36 simultaneous stand combinations. Those observed distances are not continuous maxima, material thicknesses, body-size tolerances or full Hausdorff results. Separately, a same-owner retained convex reference supplies the listed conservative bounds for all points through all rigid owner poses, with a 0.002 mm numerical allowance. Both kinds of evidence and their limits remain distinct.\n\nThe second-stage selector was independently run twice in a fresh directory containing only the unchanged selector source and the exact detailed collision JSON from the already verified first-stage source rebuild. Both outputs are byte-identical to the proposed sidecar. Generated collision JSON is explicitly a second-stage dependency, not an original source-only input. All 3,251 previously bound asset/review files and all 59 accepted production bindings remain exact.\n\n## Integration advice\n\nSelect the optional subset explicitly for coarse body contact where its stated omissions are acceptable. Preserve the original movement roots. Keep the detailed profiles and marker API available for mechanism, precise tool, grip/control and service targeting; do not silently replace them or stack both selections on the same body-collision role. The selector rejects a changed base hash.\n\nNo engine adoption, interaction implementation, load constraint, species fit, host-route acceptance or runtime performance benefit is established. The original 43/56-shape detailed proposals remain authoritative when these omissions are unsuitable.\n'''
